GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_DesignTradeoffs> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_DesignTradeoffs> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#DesignTradeoffs> ;
    narr:childCount "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "bb6d44fa6cc965e66aa05e25f3558caef9d1e0ec" ;
    narr:narration """This region holds one delivery-routing trade-off, all dated to a single ruling window. The chosen approach is [one bundle per run per person rather than one message per skill](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2), with the bundle's close condition fixed as [the run closing, late skills waiting for the next run rather than sending on their own](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4). The rejected alternative stays expandable: [per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the reader](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5). The choice was contested in the record itself — [a pushback on the batching window, held against](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3) — so the dissent is retrievable beside the verdict. The parent frame states the aim as [shielding recipients from fragmentation](narr:Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling). One decision point, not an arc.""" ;
    narr:reaction """One correction moved the picture: the prior narration anchored the rejected alternative to the wrong child — the close-condition ruling actually lives in [the run-closing rule](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4), and [the rejected per-skill alternative](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5) is its own node. The [pushback held against](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3) and the [bundling verdict](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2) are unchanged; the substance of the region held, the anchors now point where the record does.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "we route every reaction through one bundle per run per person, not one\n> message per skill — a person should get one thing to read, not four" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Tina pushed back on the batching window" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "the bundle closes when\nthe run closes, and a skill that misses the close waits for the next run rather\nthan sending on its own." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The alternative considered and rejected was per-skill\ndelivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the\nreader." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Reaction delivery bundles strictly per run per person to shield recipients from fragmentation" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The batching window was contested in the record — a pushback on when the bundle closes, held against rather than resolved by argument." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The rejected alternative (per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing) remains expandable, not erased — a road not taken whose trade-off is stated, not dismissed." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "style" ; narr:reading "antithesis-first with parallel phrasing — the sentence names what it is by naming what it isn't" ; narr:text "we route every reaction through one bundle per run per person, not one\n> message per skill — a person should get one thing to read, not four" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "register" ; narr:reading "plain-spoken when ruling, technical when describing the rejected mechanism" ; narr:text "The alternative considered and rejected was per-skill\ndelivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the\nreader." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "value" ; narr:reading "recipient-centered — the justification routes through the reader's burden, not the system's" ; narr:text "a person should get one thing to read, not four" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "power" ; narr:reading "legitimate authority exercised by holding a line, not by argument — the pushback is recorded and overruled" ; narr:text "Tina pushed back on the batching window and Tanya held: the bundle closes when\nthe run closes, and a skill that misses the close waits for the next run rather\nthan sending on its own." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "temporal" ; narr:reading "abstract and forward-looking in the ruling, concrete and past-tense when recounting the contest" ; narr:text "Tina pushed back on the batching window" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "relational" ; narr:reading "authority-ranking — decisions stated from position, dissent noted but not negotiated" ; narr:text "the bundle closes when\nthe run closes, and a skill that misses the close waits for the next run rather\nthan sending on its own." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ] ;
